// BlockDefs.inc - Single source of truth for all block definitions
// This file is consumed via X-Macro pattern in Blocks.hpp, BlockRegistry.cpp,
// and SectionDataUnpacker.cpp. Do NOT include this file directly.
//
// BLOCK_DEF(EnumName, "model_name", "Display Name", RenderLayer)
//   RenderLayer: Opaque (solid), Cutout (alpha-test), Translucent (blended)
//
// To add a new block, add a single line here. It will automatically:
//   1. Create a BlockID::EnumName enum value
//   2. Register it in BlockRegistry with the given model and render layer
//   3. Map "minecraft:model_name" to BlockID::EnumName in SectionDataUnpacker
//
// The RenderLayer must follow MC's ItemBlockRenderTypes.TYPE_BY_BLOCK: a block
// absent from that map is SOLID, one mapped to CUTOUT/CUTOUT_MIPPED is Cutout,
// TRANSLUCENT is Translucent. It matters more than it used to: the opaque
// pass draws with NO alpha test (shaders/block_opaque*.frag), so an Opaque
// block whose model samples transparent texels — cactus, the sculk sensors'
// tendrils, the copper bars/chains/lanterns, a comparator's torches — renders
// those texels as solid colour. Every such block is Cutout in MC as well.
// grass_block is the deliberate exception: MC has it in CUTOUT for its side
// overlay alone; here it stays Opaque (and occluding) and the mesher routes
// just the overlay quads to cutout (FaceDef::cutoutOverlay).
// Leaves are Cutout here and move to the opaque pass under Fast graphics at
// mesh time (Mesher::EnsureBlockPropsCache), exactly as MC's `cutoutLeaves`.

